abstract: >-
  A Harbor-native diagnostic and evaluation suite for studying how coding-agent
  harnesses mediate software-engineering execution under controlled task and
  model conditions. Version 0.2.0 contains six focused Batchline tasks plus a
  composed maintenance scenario, reusable Harbor runtime and harness integration
  utilities, deterministic verifiers and workspace observers, normalized
  execution telemetry, retained run evidence, verifier provenance, and an active
  research layer for trajectory-level analysis.
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - agent harnesses
  - software engineering
  - evaluation
  - Harbor
  - trajectory analysis
  - software testing
